            <ArticleTitle>Neurofibromatosis type II: a rare neurocutaneous syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>376-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurocutaneous syndromes are heterogeneous group of disorders with abnormalities of central as well as peripheral nervous system. Neurofibromatosis type II (NF-II) is an autosomal dominant neurocutaneous syndrome rarely diagnosed in pediatric population. Diagnosis is based on clinical history and radioimaging. We present a 14 years old boy with headache and decreased hearing, who turned to be a case of neurofibromatosis type II.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
